## Testing in Postman

The seed data includes `riya@example.com` (customer), `suresh@example.com`
(approved provider), and `admin@homeease.com` (admin). All seeded
passwords are the literal text `password`.

### 1. Login

```
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "riya@example.com",
  "password": "password"
}
```

Response will include a `token`. Copy it.

### 2. Hit a protected endpoint

```
GET http://localhost:8081/api/providers
Authorization: Bearer <paste-token-here>
```

You should get the list of three providers.

### 3. Test the admin-only approve

Log in as `admin@homeease.com` first to get an admin token, then:

```
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/providers/3/approve
Authorization: Bearer <admin-token>
```

Should return the now-approved Deepa Nair.

